WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.409 --> 00:00:10.889
So molybdenum is an element which is essential
to life and most organisms beginning with

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:17.000
you and me and going down to bacteria have
enzymes that contain molybdenum. One of the

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.730
most important enzymes is so called nitrogenase
which is an enzyme that will turn nitrogen

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:31.279
into ammonia, and nitrogenase is found in
various bacteria that live in the roots of

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:40.239
plants like beans. So the beans, via these
bacteria, can absorb nitrogen into the atmosphere

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:46.379
and turn it into a form that we can digest
and we need that nitrogen so that we can make

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:50.399
the proteins in our body. So without molybdenum
nothing could live.

